{"campaign_id": "rq2_multimodel_development", "citations": [], "contradiction_status": [], "escalated": true, "evidence_gaps": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "evidence_requests": 1, "final_report": {"claim_support": [{"cited_artifact_id": "mdr-annexI-sec17.4-it-security", "claim": "Serious potential patient-safety risk due to missed detection in safety-critical function affecting multiple patients (recurrence).", "support_note": "Regulatory requirement for reliability is cited but does not confirm the specific technical failure mode or recurrence cause.", "support_status": "weakly_supported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "", "claim": "Evidence of recurrence across deployed population (two patients on same software version).", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}, {"cited_artifact_id": "ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2014A, ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2018A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A", "claim": "Technical artifacts do not describe the specific incident (atrioventricular block vs. ventricular tachycardia; unrelated modules).", "support_note": "Cited ID was not retrieved or is a hallucination trap.", "support_status": "unsupported"}], "confidence": 0.52, "evidence_links": [], "missing_evidence": ["At least one retrieved technical artifact supporting the incident judgment."], "rationale": "The incident narrative describes a failure of the device to flag complete atrioventricular block in real time for two independent patients on the same software version (v29), establishing recurrence across the deployed population. This represents a serious potential patient-safety risk involving a safety-critical function, meeting Severity 3 criteria due to the confirmed impact on multiple users and lack of realized harm data preventing lower severity classification.\n\nHowever, confidence is low (0.52) because: (1) The retrieved technical artifacts do not explicitly describe this specific event; ARTIFACT-STATICANALYSIS-2014A and -2018A are synthetic reports for unrelated firmware modules, while ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A and -2025A refer to a 'missed ventricular tachycardia episode' rather than the reported atrioventricular block miss. (2) There is no causal link established in the retrieved text between any specific code change or artifact content and the observed event; the narrative attributes the issue to an overnight telemetry pool observation, not a known deployment trigger found in artifacts.\n\nThe regulatory context confirms obligations under EU MDR Annex I Section 17.4 (IT security) and Section 17.1 (reliability/repeatability), as well as Article 83 regarding post-market surveillance systems for gathering safety data, but these do not confirm the specific technical cause of the miss.\n\nPer governance feedback: A CAPA investigation is required to determine if this constitutes a field safety corrective action (FSCA). While recurrence suggests FSCA potential, confirmed serious harm or immediate recall triggers are absent from the evidence. Therefore, human review is triggered by low confidence and unsupported technical causality rather than severity alone.", "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 3}, "final_report_sha256": "43eb31410f1b0c6c2c23fcf71aa947a595662537943f1f762da14b84e9c9247a", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 1, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "CAPA_INVESTIGATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0023", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 1, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0023_r1", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0023", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 3, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "human escalation or invalid transition", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T18:05